WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.272
In the palace of Western Han lived a beautiful palace lady named Wang Zhaojun.

00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:06.422
She also played the pipa beautifully.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:10.492
Everyone in the palace said her pipa playing was as moving as moonlight.

00:00:10.842 --> 00:00:14.922
The Xiongnu's Huhanye Chanyu came to Han, hoping the two sides would be joined by marriage.

00:00:15.272 --> 00:00:18.320
Wang Zhaojun was chosen, and would marry into the Xiongnu.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.750
At the frontier pass, she looked back toward her homeland and bid it a reluctant farewell.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.132
She dried her tears, straightened her back, and walked forward bravely.

00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:31.562
The carriage train crossed the boundless grasslands, heading north.

00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:36.304
The wind and sand were fierce along the way, yet her heart grew calmer and calmer.

00:00:36.654 --> 00:00:42.342
The Chanyu welcomed her in person; the two bowed to each other, in a solemn and friendly atmosphere.

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:46.652
From then on, exchanges between the two peoples gradually grew more frequent.

00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:49.762
Under the sunset, wild geese flew across the sky.

00:00:50.112 --> 00:00:53.592
Wang Zhaojun's story became a beloved tale handed down through the ages.

00:00:53.942 --> 00:00:57.734
Her courage and beauty have been praised from generation to generation.

